      "@electric-sql/experimental": "$@electric-sql/experimental"
    }
  },
  "devRemarks": {
    "nothing": "now",
    "electric-sql": "pglite-sync 0.6.12 depends on @electric-sql/client and experimental ^1.0.9, which resolve to the ancient 1.0.14 with the stream pause/resume machinery (FetchError: pause-stream crash loops during heavy syncs, see https://github.com/electric-sql/pglite/issues). The override forces pglite-sync onto the root client 1.5.28 / experimental 6.0.28 where that machinery no longer exists; without it npm nests a private 1.0.14 copy under pglite-sync that the root upgrade never reaches. Drop the override once pglite-sync depends on the new versions itself.",
    "tabster": "errors were caused. tabster@8.7.0 bundled its own keyborg@2.6.0 which conflicted with the top-level keyborg@2.14.0 required by @fluentui/react-components — keyborg 2.14 removed getNavigating, so forcing tabster@8.8.0 (which depends on keyborg@^2.14.0) eliminates the nested copy and makes both packages use the same API.",
    "typescript-eslint": "eslint cannot run on typescript@7 (native) yet, so the overrides pin its peer to typescript@6.0.3 — full details in the header of scripts/patch-eslint-typescript.mjs. Drop overrides + typescript-v6 + postinstall once typescript-eslint supports v7."
  }
}
